        "path": "packages/platejs/src/markdown/lib/table.spec.ts",
        "sha256": "785c5baf76a0d338f89a4f7c59c335e42021b4e5a17dc248f57b90ec0e2a5fc0",
        "claim": "A ragged GFM table parses to exactly the committed document; fails without padding."
      }
    ],
    "limits": "Working tree only, nothing committed. React still re-renders every block per publication (a stable view needs a document-dependency mechanism that works in RSC). Only the table correction was checked for parse/commit divergence. Projection-2's snapshot predates the table padding, so its CJK 50 KB text parity comes from the headless receipt. pnpm test fails the same 27 tests as before this change: 26 also fail at HEAD, and one schema-construction timing budget passes alone."
  },
